WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.920
Happy Star Wars Friday, everybody.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.020
So we've got some really cool Kylo Ren / Rey stuff to break down

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.960
and I'll explain a couple really important dates.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.460
We got new Jedi costumes,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.360
We've got to talk about Rey's parents

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.680
Daisy Ridley said some really pointed stuff that erased a whole bunch of theories

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.540
that actually gives her a couple things in common with the Snoke character

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.780
at least with the way that they were created.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.160
Star Wars Day, which is coming up next week, new footage stuff dropping

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.460
and then Episode IX Carrie Fisher and Rian Johnson returning stuff.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.000
So let's start with the costume stuff,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.420
but there is a new round of the Star Wars giveaway

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.640
all you have to do to enter is be a subscriber and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.540
It's just for a copy of the Rogue One Blu-Ray.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.440
So if you ever wanted a reason to buy Star Wars video games,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.920
it would be to get a peek at what's coming up in the new films

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.820
because the Battlefront II Star Wars stuff revealed what Rey's Jedi costume

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.180
and Kylo Ren's new costume is going to look like.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.400
And I know there was a bunch of people talking about Kylo Ren's scargate stuff

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.540
I'll address that, but it's not that big a deal.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.620
There was a funny answer that Rian Johnson had,

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.020
he made a big change to the way Kylo Ren's scar looks on his face.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:07.080
So if you remember, back during Force Awakens, in their fight,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.440
Daisy Ridley slashed him, and he had this big cut going down the bridge of his nose.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.240
So when we got to The Last Jedi trailer,

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.440
a lot of people were like, 'hey wait a minute, why does Kylo Ren's scar look so different?'

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.480
and he probably could have healed that in a Bacta tank

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.880
So there's just a number of questions that people had about the look of his face,

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.020
in addition to his new costume.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.240
So the answer is that Rian Johnson said that when they were filming,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.260
the scar going down the bridge of his nose just looked stupid.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.760
So, "I wanted to change it because it looked weird," which I think is a fine reason

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.200
But you can see the costume, both his and Rey's, just have a lot more color.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.780
Rey is slowly moving toward the Jedi brown

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.700
which makes you wonder if she's on the Luke Skywalker path

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.240
from going to relatively colorless costume in the first movie,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.080
to Jedi brown in the second movie,

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:10.180
and then winding up where Luke Skywalker ended up in Return of the Jedi, with like a full black costume.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.120
You go the whole gamut.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.680
And I know they're implying that there's a lot of darkness in The Last Jedi,

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.720
just because of all the red color in the trailer,

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.240
and the way they did the poster,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.620
and there's even a crazy new rumor that Luke Skywalker has been keeping Darth Vader's kyber crystal,

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:28.040
the red crystal, hanging around his neck, and Kylo Ren really wants it.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.320
So before I address that big rumor, just let me know what you think about their new costumes.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.040
It just seems like Kylo Ren is going to be spending a lot more time without his mask on,

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.360
because most of the pictures we've seen him in, relative to Episode IIX, show him without it,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.220
and it's even smashed in the trailer,

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:48.760
so either it was destroyed after his fight with Rey, or he destroyed it himself in his own rage.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:54.360
Because it does seem like he breaks a lot of his own stuff. You just see him destroying consoles left and right

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.900
But obviously he's dressed a lot more like Anakin Skywalker was from Revenge of the Sith.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:04.540
So I love how even though he's moving away from Darth Vader because he's not wearing that mask anymore,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.040
he is still very much trying to emulate the path of Anakin Skywalker.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:13.100
George Lucas never fully explained why it was that Anakin chose these darker colors,

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.600
but visually it was just meant to foreshadow what was going to be coming for him,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.720
like you all know that he's turning into Darth Vader,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.040
so wouldn't it make sense that he'd have some darker tendencies that would show themselves

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.960
in the way he dressed and the things that he did, the way he acted.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:29.380
But I think part of the reason people are so upset about Kylo Ren,

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.840
in addition to him being written in a really beta way,

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.940
is the fact that he doesn't seem to have a personality of his own.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.960
He's just trying to co-opt Darth Vader's personality, like he's this young teenager who's lost his way,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:44.560
so he sees this iconic figure that he finds out that he's related to, so he's like,

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.920
"Oh my god, I'm going to be just like that. I'm going to do exactly what he did."

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.620
So you never really find out who Ben Solo was.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:56.440
You only know who the faux Anakin Skywalker/Darth Vader is, walking around in this makeshift mask.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.160
But if you're not a huge fan of the character,

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.900
the cool thing is is that Adam Driver did say that they would explore some of his humanity,

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.260
so you'd find a little bit about what's going on in his head during Episode IIX.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.820
Even though most of the focus has now shifted off of him onto Luke Skywalker,

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.780
because people are like, 'what is going on with this crazy person?"

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.040
'"The Jedi need to end"? That is the craziest thing that has ever come out of your mouth.'

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.940
But, Luke Skywalker as Rey's father -- so that was one of the biggest theories,

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.520
So we've got to talk about Rey's parents.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.420
That's like the next big thing that they kind of unofficially revealed,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.760
or at least cut a bunch of theories out,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.600
So a bunch of you messaged me after they dropped the trailer, they did the big panel,

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.760
asking about these two things, like, 'hey, are they actually confirming this?'

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.280
So there was a later interview that Daisy Ridley did that I'll play in a second.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:47.380
This was Josh Gad making jokes onstage about trying to get them to reveal who Rey's parents were.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.240
"Rey Skywalker?" "Rey Kenobi?"

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.660
Are you and Luke related by blood?

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.720
No to that one, okay.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.240
Are you a Skywalker?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.360
Is your name Rey Skywalker?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.260
Is your name Rey Kenobi?

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.700
That's a popular answer, clearly.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.960
Who doesn't know their own last name?

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:20.680
So the important thing to remember about that is that Star Wars secrecy is so hardcore

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.200
that all of that is carefully choreographed,

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.060
they tell him what he's allowed to make jokes about before they go out there,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:30.880
and I don't think they'd let him kae that joke if there was even a small chance

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.000
that Rey was either a Kenobi or a Skywalker.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.040
Now the interview that Daisy Ridley did provides some even better evidence,

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.380
so I'm going to play this clip here, and then I'll explain what that means.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:46.140
So how is Rey's relationship in this movie different than Luke's relationship with, say, Yoda or Obi-Wan?

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.020
Um, well, Rey is not a teacher.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:54.420
Yoda and Obi-Wan are very much, like, guiding figures in Luke's life

00:05:54.900 --> 00:06:00.260
and, um, Rey, I think, obviously he doesn't even know who she is when she turns up,

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:03.700
like, with this frickin' lightsaber that he's not seen in however long

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:09.280
so that in itself is a big difference, and then as things go on, I think there's an expectation,

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.760
there's always been an expectation on Luke as to his potential and what he can do or what he should do,

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:18.300
much like with Rey, so in that sense they're kind of similar, but obviously the dynamic has changed

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.400
because she's expecting something from him this time,

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:25.580
and it remains to be seen, whether, you know, how he reacts to that.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.040
So I know it sounds like she's making a couple off-handed remarks

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.560
about the initial meeting with Luke Skywalker

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:35.360
He's never seen her before, he has no idea, "Who are you?"

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:41.560
That does not sound like something that a father who's being reunited with his child would say at all.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:43.960
"Who are you? I've never seen you before."

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:48.660
So that also means that she probably wasn't a student at his Jedi academy.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.120
The way they're presenting Luke Skywalker is that he was kind of a failure

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.480
when everybody had these big hopes for him after the Empire fell

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:58.660
but that's some pretty damning evidence, if he doesn't know who she is,

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:05.120
and he has that crazy force connection to his sister Leia, he would know if she had another child with Han Solo,

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.680
and she were a Solo, so she'd still be part Skywalker in that case.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:13.520
But now it just sounds like there's much more evidence that she is a completely new character

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:14.660
that we've never met before.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.260
That doesn't mean that she's not related to someone in the Star Wars universe, it just implies that she's not

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.120
related to the people that you would think that she would be related to.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:27.300
So the big thing now that she has in common with the Snoke character is that they both seem like

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:30.940
brand new characters that you've never met before in the Star Wars universe.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:36.140
And even though they keep reiterating that this is very much a story about the Skywalker family,

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:41.020
the Skywalker part of that story looks like it's coming through the Ben Solo character

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.260
So I know everybody really wanted Rey to be part of the Skywalker family, or even Obi-Wan,

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:50.020
so you have this really nice unbroken line of Skywalker lineage from Anakin Skywalker,

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:52.900
but most of that is flowing through the Ben Solo character,

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:58.560
and Rey, just like the MacGuffin, the Journal of the Whills in the trailer, is representative of

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.000
the new thing that they're bringing in, the new way they're headed.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:08.340
So you have this idea of just recycling old content, recylcing old Darth Vader in Ben Solo.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.540
We need something new, something fresh.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:16.120
So practically, during the plot of the movie, as well as metaphorically in the Star Wars expanded universe,

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.400
like them actually making these movies, they need to inject fresh things,

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:23.760
So you have the Journal of the Whills helping contextualize Star Wars mythology

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:24.820
within the story,

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:29.160
and then you have the Rey character, someone new to take that path.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:33.340
This was all part of Mark Hamill talking a lot about how it's not Luke's story anymore,

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.500
and then Kathleen Kennedy jumped out and was like, "But Luke is still a very important part of this."

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.480
Like she didn't want him to downplay Luke's importance in the story

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:45.480
So the Skywalkers are still a very big part of the direction that the Star Wars galaxy is headed

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:48.900
But you'll probably see, once they start announcing more spinoff movies,

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:52.060
and whatever trilogy is going to come next after Episode IX,

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:56.080
is that they'll start moving past the idea of the lineage of Darth Vader

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.520
But let me know, just based on Daisy Ridley's comments and Luke Skywalker not knowing who she is,

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.400
who do you think her parents are?

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:07.120
Are they completely new characters, which is what it seems like they're implying,

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.200
or do you think it's somebody else inside the Star Wars universe?

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.920
So I know you're all wondering when we're going to see new footage,

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:17.900
the next big Star Wars day is May the 4th, Star Wars Day, may the Fourth be with you.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:23.340
they will definitely be promoting Star Wars on that day, but there hasn't been any confirmation of new footage

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.240
I'm not expecting a new trailer.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:30.360
So if they do drop new video content, it's more likely that it would be behind the scenes stuff

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:35.400
which is still very revealing, we learned a whole bunch of stuff from The Force Awakens behind the scenes reel

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:41.360
and D23 is happening later this summer, like the week or two before Comic Con happens,

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:44.480
and they'll probably be presenting more Star Wars footage.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:50.720
They usually don't release that D23 footage to the public, but during the last D23 during a Star Wars year,

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:55.560
they did air Force Awakens content, so I'm expecting them to do the same thing for Last Jedi.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.780
And really like the last big thing is Episode IX.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.340
If you've been reading about what's going on with them developing the project,

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:05.200
Colin Trevorrow, who did Jurassic World, is directing the movie

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.900
they're working on a different treatment, Rian Johnson was originally writing a version of the script,

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.720
but they said that he's not involved with that anymore, he's just doing Episode IIX

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.700
And Kathleen Kennedy just reiterated that they're not going to have some crazy trick

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.400
to try to work Leia into Episode IX.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:25.140
So they're going to do whatever they can to honor her character, and not completely upset everyone

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:29.560
that would just freak out if they saw CG Leia in Episode IX, so don't worry about that.

